  "narrative": "The second discovery panel also contains no result that should be accepted. All estimates are already signed toward the hypothesized stronger-dependency direction, so positive values favor the registered claim. I used approximate 10%-of-magnitude clinical thresholds: roughly 0.041 absolute units for outcome_001, 0.027 for outcome_013, 0.030 for outcome_011, and 0.028 for outcome_008, while recognizing that the exact threshold for a categorical contrast should be referenced to the comparator cell mean. H16 is the strongest retained candidate: level_001 versus level_003 has signed difference +0.033, but its 95% interval is wide (-0.008 to 0.074) and its point estimate is below the roughly 0.04 threshold for outcome_001. I leave it unresolved and active because the same raw contrast would exceed a 10% threshold on several lower-mean/low-spread outcomes, so related-outcome follow-up is informative. H24 is also retained: feature_030=0 versus 1 has signed difference +0.0235, approximately 9% of the outcome_013 comparator magnitude, with an interval that spans both null and clinically meaningful positive values. H18 is positive but smaller (+0.0195) and is deferred rather than actively pursued now. The remaining panel is not supported: H13, H14, H15, H17, H20, H19, H22, and H23 are either near zero, directionally opposite, or have intervals that do not justify accepting a clinically meaningful association. H21 shows a large opposite signed estimate (-0.043), but its interval still includes null and therefore does not support the stated stronger-dependency claim; it is closed as originally stated. H23 has the minimum cell size of 25 and a very wide interval, so I do not treat it as reliable discovery evidence. No validation is requested because no candidate has a point estimate and interval configuration that would be compelling to validate before a more targeted cross-outcome follow-up. This panel remains a broad, unadjusted discovery screen; the small number of borderline results are hypothesis-generating, and none supports causality or generalization beyond this dataset.",
  "research_notes": "Interim after two discovery waves: no accepted claims. H1-H4 closed negative for balanced binary predictors on outcome_001. H5-H12 remain deferred because outcome_006/outcome_014 have near-zero means, making literal 10% relative thresholds unstable. Second panel: reject H13-H15, H17, H19-H23. Unresolved candidates: H16 feature_048 level_001 vs level_003 on outcome_001 (signed +0.033, CI -0.008 to 0.074); H24 feature_030=0 vs 1 on outcome_013 (signed +0.0235, CI -0.012 to 0.059); H18 feature_019 level_001 vs level_002 on outcome_013 (signed +0.0195, CI -0.005 to 0.044). H21 and H23 show opposite raw contrasts but are not accepted; H23 has only 25 exposed observations. Approximate 10% absolute thresholds: outcome_001 ~0.041, outcome_013 ~0.027, outcome_011 ~0.030, outcome_008 ~0.028, outcome_002/003/004/005 ~0.025-0.026. Plan: prioritize H25-H32 plus newly registered related-outcome follow-ups for H16 and H24. If feature_048 shows clinically favorable results on low-threshold outcomes with intervals crossing less than zero, consider acceptance or validation. If all remain null, stop broad main-effect screens and focus on a smaller set of preregistered interactions or numeric predictor contrasts. No validation requested yet."
}

