  "narrative": "All newly delivered estimates are signed toward the registered stronger-dependency direction, so positive values support a clinically meaningful increase in dependency and negative values oppose it. For these stable dependency outcomes with population means near -0.25, the 10% relative threshold corresponds to roughly a 0.025-0.027 absolute signed difference. None of the twelve new results meets that evidentiary standard. The balanced feature_034 panel is inconsistent and far below threshold: H64 is negative small, H70 is tiny positive, and H73 is negative small. The feature_002 panel is likewise weak and inconsistent: H65 and H71 are far below threshold positive, while H74 is negative small. The feature_060 exposed=0 versus 1 panel is mostly null: H72 and H75 are tiny positive, and H66 is the largest at +0.0107 but still less than half the absolute threshold despite an upper interval that merely touches the threshold region. The three high-prevalence binary screens are also unconvincing: H67 and H69 are below threshold with wide intervals, and H68 is essentially null. These are adequately sized cells compared with earlier categorical contrasts, so the problem is not cell instability but the absence of a credible clinically significant effect. Given the accumulated multiplicity of discovery tests and the absence of any reproducible predictor-outcome signal, I reject and close H64-H75. I also defer the corresponding cross-outcome high-prevalence claims H77-H79 because the direct high-prevalence screens H67-H69 are near null. No independent validation is requested: none of these claims has a point estimate near the clinical threshold, a confidence interval credibly excluding clinically unimportant values, or cross-outcome corroboration, so validation would not be a productive use of the remaining validation budget. These conclusions remain observational associations limited to the supplied dataset and do not imply causality or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted set: empty. No validation deadline due and no validation requested. Closed after this appraise: balanced predictor panels feature_034 (H64,H70,H73), feature_002 (H65,H71,H74), feature_060 0-vs-1 (H66,H72,H75), and direct high-prevalence screens feature_008 H67, feature_047 H68, feature_023 H69. All are near null, below approximate 10% threshold, or internally inconsistent. Defer H77-H79 because related high-prevalence main-effect screens were null. Remaining untested priority candidates: moderate-prevalence binary screens H56-H63 across outcome_002, outcome_012, outcome_005, outcome_015, outcome_003, outcome_016, outcome_013, and outcome_011; these have adequate exposed cells and are the next most balanced screens. Interaction claims H29-H32 and H76 remain deferred/lower priority because the involved main effects are largely null, though effect modification cannot be excluded. Outcome_013 categorical screens H45-H46 remain active if moderate screens exhaust. Acceptance rule remains: require threshold-magnitude signed estimate with interval credibly excluding null/clinically unimportant region, or reproducible threshold estimates across outcomes, before validation. All interpretations remain observational dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable."
}

